# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# /opt/start.sh boots Vault (file backend), initializes + unseals it, and writes
# a secret so /vault/data holds real on-disk storage, then execs `sleep infinity`.
# The vulnerability (world/group-readable /vault/data) is fixed with a chmod that
# needs no restart, so there is no "forgot to restart" case. PID 1 stays sleep.
